The result follows from the Liénard (relativistic Larmor) formula applied to each charge, noting that for the circular motion \( \mathbf v\!\perp\!\mathbf a\) the radiated power per charge is invariant under a boost parallel to the axis, while the charge density transforms as \(\rho'=\gamma_{\beta}\rho\); the integration over the cross‑section gives the expression above.  (Valid for \(\omega R<c\)).
